WEBVTT

00:00:00.134 --> 00:00:03.259
{fluent}Hello, and a very warm welcome to Shah Spectrum.

00:00:03.259 --> 00:00:05.246
If you're new here, welcome.

00:00:05.246 --> 00:00:10.019
If you're back again, it's lovely to have you with us once more.

00:00:10.636 --> 00:00:12.752
Americans have just voted.

00:00:12.752 --> 00:00:18.427
Within a day, the Dow Jones had its biggest gain of the year, oil was hovering near

00:00:18.427 --> 00:00:23.189
a hundred dollars a barrel, and India's share market hit a two-month high.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:25.769
Did one election really do all that?

00:00:26.549 --> 00:00:30.966
Hi, I'm Mittal Shah, and today I'll take you through what really moved, and what

00:00:30.966 --> 00:00:32.444
only looks connected.

00:00:32.444 --> 00:00:33.905
{fluent}The result is in.

00:00:33.905 --> 00:00:39.819
Democrats have won control of both chambers of the United States Congress, the House

00:00:39.819 --> 00:00:41.668
of Representatives and the Senate.

00:00:41.668 --> 00:00:46.180
This was a midterm election, held halfway through President Donald Trump's four-year

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:46.780
term.

00:00:46.408 --> 00:00:51.498
In the Senate, reports count Democrats at about fifty-four of the hundred seats.

00:00:51.498 --> 00:00:57.274
A few races are still too close to call, and the size of their House majority is

00:00:57.274 --> 00:00:58.187
still being counted.

00:00:58.187 --> 00:01:01.611
The new Congress takes its seats on the third of January.

00:01:01.611 --> 00:01:03.530
So no law has changed yet.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:06.820
What has changed is what everyone expects.

00:01:07.661 --> 00:01:09.109
Start with how laws get made.

00:01:09.109 --> 00:01:12.211
A bill needs both chambers and the president's signature.

00:01:12.211 --> 00:01:15.313
Trump has said he will veto everything he opposes.

00:01:15.313 --> 00:01:20.219
To override a veto, Congress needs two thirds of both chambers, and Democrats are

00:01:20.219 --> 00:01:22.716
well short of that.

00:01:22.716 --> 00:01:27.746
So they cannot simply cancel tariffs, the taxes on imported goods, over his head.

00:01:28.526 --> 00:01:30.751
What they can do is use the budget.

00:01:30.751 --> 00:01:35.011
Congress writes the spending bills, and if those are not agreed, parts of the

00:01:35.011 --> 00:01:37.060
government can run out of money.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:41.158
That gives Democrats leverage in every negotiation.

00:01:41.158 --> 00:01:46.235
Analysts have a word for a Congress and a president who can block each other:

00:01:46.235 --> 00:01:46.835
gridlock.

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:52.450
Some Democrats have also promised to try to limit the Iran war, including by

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:53.816
restricting its funding.

00:01:53.816 --> 00:01:58.893
But the president still controls defence and foreign policy, so that fight will be

00:01:58.893 --> 00:01:59.493
slow.

00:02:00.375 --> 00:02:01.313
Now the markets.

00:02:01.313 --> 00:02:06.070
On Wednesday the Dow jumped nearly sixteen hundred points, about three per cent.

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:10.289
Why would investors cheer a result that weakens the president's party?

00:02:10.289 --> 00:02:10.967
Analysts offered two reasons.

00:02:10.967 --> 00:02:14.476
First, the uncertainty is over.

00:02:14.476 --> 00:02:18.823
One analyst said investors are happy to have the midterms out of the way.

00:02:18.823 --> 00:02:23.191
Second, gridlock makes sweeping changes to tax and spending harder, and markets

00:02:23.191 --> 00:02:25.099
often like fewer surprises.

00:02:25.099 --> 00:02:30.918
That is an explanation analysts offer, not a law of nature.

00:02:30.918 --> 00:02:32.638
And not everyone gained.

00:02:32.638 --> 00:02:37.649
Companies tied to building AI data centres were under pressure, as investors

00:02:37.649 --> 00:02:41.521
wondered whether Democratic wins in Texas could slow that building.

00:02:42.266 --> 00:02:44.856
Oil moved too, and this matters more for us.

00:02:44.856 --> 00:02:49.984
Brent crude, the world's main oil price benchmark, slipped to just over a hundred

00:02:49.984 --> 00:02:51.168
dollars a barrel.

00:02:51.168 --> 00:02:56.921
Since just before the war with Iran began, it has swung between roughly seventy and

00:02:56.921 --> 00:02:58.147
a hundred and twenty dollars.

00:02:58.147 --> 00:03:00.889
We cannot say the election cut the price.

00:03:00.889 --> 00:03:06.896
Talks between the United States and Iran are continuing, and one Iranian official

00:03:06.896 --> 00:03:10.322
said the two sides remain some distance from a deal.

00:03:10.322 --> 00:03:13.749
So treat the link between the vote and oil as unproven.

00:03:14.524 --> 00:03:16.666
Here is where India comes in.

00:03:16.666 --> 00:03:22.081
India buys most of its oil from abroad, so cheaper oil eases pressure on the import

00:03:22.081 --> 00:03:24.174
bill, the rupee and prices at home.

00:03:24.174 --> 00:03:29.738
On Wednesday the Nifty, the index of India's fifty large listed companies, closed

00:03:29.738 --> 00:03:31.464
near twenty-four thousand.

00:03:31.464 --> 00:03:36.990
That is a two-month high, and about five and a half per cent up in five sessions.

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:41.362
Foreign portfolio investors, meaning overseas funds that buy Indian shares, played a

00:03:41.362 --> 00:03:41.962
part.

00:03:41.608 --> 00:03:47.585
They sold about thirty-five thousand crore rupees of Indian shares in October, but

00:03:47.585 --> 00:03:52.014
have bought nearly fifteen thousand crore in the last five sessions.

00:03:52.014 --> 00:03:55.901
Easing oil and returning foreign money are the reasons most reports give.

00:03:56.726 --> 00:03:58.157
What do we not know?

00:03:58.157 --> 00:03:59.798
The final seat counts.

00:03:59.798 --> 00:04:01.521
Whether oil keeps falling.

00:04:01.521 --> 00:04:05.947
And how the new Congress and the president behave once January arrives.

00:04:05.947 --> 00:04:08.680
Any of these can change the picture quickly.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:09.715
{fluent}To sum up:

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:12.349
the vote itself has changed no law yet.

00:04:12.349 --> 00:04:16.486
What moved markets was expectation, mixed with cheaper oil.

00:04:16.486 --> 00:04:21.016
What lasts will depend on what Congress and the president actually do.

00:04:21.879 --> 00:04:27.492
Before you go, we looked at what was at stake in this election on the third of

00:04:27.492 --> 00:04:29.958
November, in our episode 'US midterms:

00:04:29.958 --> 00:04:32.618
why the result matters for the economy'.

00:04:32.618 --> 00:04:34.589
The link is in the description.

00:04:34.589 --> 00:04:37.584
Thanks for listening, and see you in the next episode!

